<newsitem itemid="79784" id="root" date="1996-09-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>SWITZERLAND: Zurich details first-time H1 results.</title>
<headline>Zurich details first-time H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     576.4	     vs 434.2</p>
<p> Net per share, Sfr	   12.70	     vs n/a</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit		 944.7	     vs 735.7</p>
<p> Underwriting result	  2,104.9	   vs 1,819.0</p>
<p> Taxes			    355.8	     vs 279.1</p>
<p> Gross premiums		 16,563.2	  vs 14,993.0</p>
<p> Net premiums		   13,473.3	  vs 12,012.1</p>
<p> Net losses incurred	  11,351.5	  vs 10,305.3</p>
<p> Policy holder's dividends  640.7	     vs 689.6</p>
<p> Net underwrite expenses    3,492.4	   vs 2,947.7</p>
<p> Investment income	    3,083.1	   vs 2,545.2</p>
<p> Interest expense	     166.8	     vs 149.4</p>
<p> Write-downs		    174.2	     vs 68.8</p>
<p> Realised investment gains  672.7	     vs 286.0</p>
<p> Unrealised investment gain 810.5	     vs 1,046.3</p>
<p> Write-down on goodwill     36.6		vs zero</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Zurich Insurance Co. This is the first time Zurich has presented six month consolidated results based on the same accounting principles as full-year results.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
